      <div type="clause" n="2.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 2.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.2" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="280" ed="#liebermann"/>Þonne is swiðe rihtlic, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> Godes ciricgrið<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.10"/> binnon wagum ⁊ Cristenes ciningces<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.11"/> handgrið stande æfre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="***" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.star3"/> unwemme<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.12"/>; ⁊ se ðe aðor fulbrece, þolige landes ⁊ lifes, butan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.13"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.dagger"/> se ciningc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.14"/> gearian wylle.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.15"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.2" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="280" ed="#liebermann"/>Þonne is swiðe rihtlic, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> Godes cyricgrið binnan wagum ⁊ Crystenes cyninges handgrið<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.3-2"/> stande efen unwemmed; and se þe aðor fulbrece, ðolige landes ⁊ lifes, buton him se cyningc gearian wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.2" corresp="#wit-d-frags"><pb n="280" ed="#liebermann"/>[2, 2] Ðon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> is swiðe rihtlic, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> Godes ciricgrið binnon wágu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ⁊ Cristenes cynges handgrið stande efen unwæm<hi rend="italic">me</hi>.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.star"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="2.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="280" ed="#liebermann"/>Et ualde iustum est, ut ęcclesię pax intra parietes suos et pax Christiani regis, quam manu sua dederit, semper<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.6"/> inuiolata<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.1"/> (inconuulsa) permaneat; quicumque alterutram<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.7"/> perfregerit, de uita et omnibus in misericordia regis sit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="2.2" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="281" ed="#liebermann"/>Quare ęquissimum est, ut pax ęcclesiarum Dei infra parietes et pax data manu Christiani<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.1-2"/> regis semper stet inuiolata; et qui aliquam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.3"/>, ęcclesię<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.4-2"/> scilicet aut regis pacem, fregerit, careat omnibus bonis suis et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.5"/> uita<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.6-2"/>, nisi rex illi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.7-2"/> parcere uoluerit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="2.2" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="281" ed="#liebermann"/>Est ergo iustissimum, ut Dei ecclesie pax et Christiani regis manus pax stet semper inuiolata; et qui utram plene infregerit, careat terra et uita, nisi ei misericordiam rex prestare uoluerit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="2.2" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="154" ed="#robertson"/>Þonne is swiðe rihtlic, þæt Godes ciricgrið binnon wagum ⁊ Cristenes ciningces handgrið stande æfre<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#ICn_2-2.robnote.fn.11"/> unwemme<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#ICn_2-2.robnote.fn.12"/>; ⁊ se ðe aðor fulbrece þolige landes ⁊ lifes, butan [him]<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#ICn_2-2.robnote.fn.13"/> se ciningc gearian wille.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="232" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Þonne is swiðe rihtlic þæt Godes ciricgrið binnon wagum and Cristenes ciningces handgrið stande æfre unwemme; and se ðe aðor fulbrece þolige landes and lifes, butan him se ciningc gearian wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="281" ed="#liebermann"/>Nun ist höchst rechtmässig, dass der von Gottes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.de.1"/> Kirche innerhalb ihrer Mauern [ausgehende] Sonderschutz und der Sonderschutz aus der Hand des christlichen Königs gleichermassen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.de.2"/> (stets <hi rend="italic">G</hi>) unverletzlich bestehe; und wer einen von beiden gänzlich<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.de.3"/> [durch Todtschlag] verletzt, verliere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.de.4"/> Land und Leben<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.de.5"/>, ausser wenn ihn der König begnadigen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_2-2.lnote.de.6"/> will.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Now it is very right that the protection of God's church within its walls and the protection given by the Christian king's own hand stand equally (always, G) inviolate; and whoever wholly breaks either [by killing], let him lose land and life, unless the king is willing to pardon him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_2-2.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="155" ed="#robertson"/>Therefore it is very right and proper that the protection given by the church of God within its walls, and the protection granted by a Christian king in person should always remain inviolate; and he who violates<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#ICn_2-2.robnote.n.2"/> either of them shall lose both land and life<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#ICn_2-2.robnote.n.3"/>, unless the king<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#ICn_2-2.robnote.n.4"/> is willing to pardon him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="233" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Accordingly, it is most proper that the sanctuary within the walls of God’s church and the protection received from the Christian king’s hand remain always inviolate; and the person who defies either of them shall forfeit land and life unless the king is willing to pardon him.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="281"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_14">VI Atr 14</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 14</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:Grith_2">Grið 2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:EGu_1">EGu 1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 2:2: Cn 1018 2:2 (HomN L) Grið 2, Pol. I 100, VI Atr 14, EGu 1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_14">VI Atr 14</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 2:2: Cn 1018 2:2 (HomN L) Grið 2, Pol. I 100, VI Atr 14, EGu 1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-008">Cn 1018 2.2</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 2:2: Cn 1018 2:2 (HomN L) Grið 2, Pol. I 100, VI Atr 14, EGu 1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:Grith_2">Grið 2</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 2:2: Cn 1018 2:2 (HomN L) Grið 2, Pol. I 100, VI Atr 14, EGu 1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#kennedy" n="59"><label>closer to (than VI Atr)</label> <ref target="clause:EGu_1">EGu 1</ref> <quote>Both D ch. 2.2 and I Cn. 2.2 are closer to E Gu 1 than to VI Æthelred: Whitelock</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#kennedy" n="59"><label>used in I–II Cnut</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-007">Cn 1018 2.1–2.2</ref> <quote>Kennedy’s table: VI Æthelred 13, VI Æthelred 14 | D 2.1–2.2 | I Cnut 2.1, I Cnut 2.2</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">G's ‘æfre’ should be corrected to ‘efen’ (EGu, I Cn D, A); Ld has ‘efer’, the Latin versions ‘semper’. ‘him’ is supplied in G from A, Ld, Cons. Cn. and Inst. Cn. Liebermann compares VI Atr 14.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 281, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">him: omitted G; supplied from A</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">280</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyr. binnan <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyr. binnan Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">280</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyninges <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyninges Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.star3" n="***" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">280</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> efen <hi rend="italic">laut EGu 1 D A;</hi> efer <hi rend="italic">Ld;</hi> semper <hi rend="italic">Versiones</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read efen as in EGu 1 D A; efer Ld; semper Versiones</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">280</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-med <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-med Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">280</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">buton <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">buton Ld</seg></note>
