        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">281</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">prāre <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">prāre Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">280</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt</hi> II Cnut 1—7, <hi rend="italic">dann</hi> I Cnut 6.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">there follow II Cnut 1—7, then I Cnut 6.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">281</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">281</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">aliquando <hi rend="italic">H;</hi> e. al. <hi rend="italic">Ct</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">aliquando H; e. al. Ct</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">281</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-siarum <hi rend="italic">Cb;</hi> -siam <hi rend="italic">Lb Ct Jo</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-siarum Cb; -siam Lb Ct Jo</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">281</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Cb;</hi> cum <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Cb; cum the rest</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">281</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sua <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Lb Ct</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sua added by Lb Ct</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">281</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">condonauerit <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> i. p. u. <hi rend="italic">Lb S Ct Jo</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">condonauerit instead of i. p. u. Lb S Ct Jo</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_2-2.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">280</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-grid <hi rend="italic">A</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-grid A</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_2-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">198</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Am Rande bessere ‘<hi rend="italic">ebd</hi>. 14’.—Hieraus Grið 2; Polity 25; <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 266. 275. Im Sinne <hi rend="italic">vgl</hi>. II Eg 5, 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">In the margin correct to ‘<hi rend="italic">ibid</hi>. 14’. — Hence Grið 2; Polity 25; <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 266. 275. For the sense <hi rend="italic">cf</hi>. II Eg 5, 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_2-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">198</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">efen</hi> Quellen und Benutzer, ausser Versionen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">efen</hi> in the sources and in the texts that use this one, except the versions</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_2-2.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">198</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">per homicidium</hi>; Hn 12, 1, im Ggs. zu <hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 3. Auch sonst (Had 4) steht Lebensverlust als ‘Vollbruch’ in Ggs. zur Halbverletzung; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi>. Totschlag an dem, der dem Beleidigten Sühne gezahlt oder angeboten hat, kostet nicht Handfrieden, sondern ‘Königschutz’; gegen Steenstrup <hi rend="italic">Danelag</hi> 362</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">per homicidium</hi>; Hn 12, 1, in contrast to <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 3. Elsewhere too (Had 4) loss of life, as ‘full breach’, stands in contrast to the half-breach; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi>. Homicide of a man who has paid or offered amends to the injured party costs not hand-peace but ‘king’s protection’; against Steenstrup <hi rend="italic">Danelag</hi> 362</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_2-2.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">198</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Unabbüssbar durch Geld; <hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 2, 3, auch III Atr 1; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> busslos 4. 5A; Begnadigung 1A</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not to be atoned for with money; <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 2, 3, also III Atr 1; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> busslos 4. 5A; Begnadigung 1A</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_2-2.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">198</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">de membris culpa</hi> Hn 79, 3. ‘Land’ steht für Vermögen überhaupt; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Vermögenseinziehung 4b</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">de membris culpa</hi> Hn 79, 3. ‘Land’ stands for property in general; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Vermögenseinziehung 4b</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_2-2.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">198</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q braucht Anglonormann. Terminus; <hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> Misericordia</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q uses an Anglo-Norman term; <hi rend="italic">see Gl</hi> Misericordia</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_2-2.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. VI Atr. 14; <hi rend="italic">Be Griðe</hi>, 2; Wulfstan, pp. 266, 275.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_2-2.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> with homicide, cf. VIII Atr. 1, 1; <hi rend="italic">Nor. Grið</hi>, 1.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_2-2.robnote.n.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. <hi rend="italic">botleas</hi>, cap. 2, 3; III Atr. 1. Forfeiture of property generally accompanies loss of life, cf. Af. 4; 4, 2; II As. 20, 3; V Pre. § 3; VI, 1, 1 and 5; IV Edg. 11; V Atr. 28 G; VI, 37; VIII, 42; II Cn. 57; DB. <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi>. 154.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_2-2.robnote.n.4" n="4" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. VIII Atr. 1, 1 and note.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_2-2.robnote.fn.11" n="11" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">154</biblScope></bibl><label>æfre</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">efen</hi> D, A.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_2-2.robnote.fn.12" n="12" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">154</biblScope></bibl><label>unwemme</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">II Cn. 1–7 follows in D.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_2-2.robnote.fn.13" n="13" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">154</biblScope></bibl><label>him</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">A, Ld, om. G.</seg></note>
